 4. Rocket Lab&#x27;s reach 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Electron launches from Rocket Lab Complex 2 on Wallops Island, Virginia. Photo: Courtesy of Rocket Lab

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump put the space rocket industry on notice in August when he set an audacious annual goal of 1,000 U.S. rocket launches and reentries by 2030 — a roughly 460% increase from last year.

 Why it matters : To meet Trump's mandate, America needs more launch sites — especially for top national security missions.

 What they're saying: The rocket industry should mirror the commercial airline business — meaning launch regulations need to change, Rocket Lab's vice president of global launch services, Brian Rogers, tells Axios. 

 Rogers said Rocket Lab gave feedback to the FAA and the Commerce Department about sticking points that hinder launch expansion. The big picture: U.S. National Security Space Launch missions are currently limited to Florida's Cape Canaveral and California's Vandenberg Space Force Base.

 Rocket Lab is expanding its footprint in Virginia and Alaska . This summer, the company unveiled GHOST : a containerized launch site that allows rockets to send payloads into orbit from anywhere. Zoom in: Rocket Lab launches its suborbital HASTE and small-lift Electron rockets from its complex at the Mid-Atlantic Regional Spaceport on Wallops Island, Virginia.

 The company said yesterday its medium-lift Neutron rocket is targeting an inaugural launch out of Wallops next year. When Neutron eventually launches for its first NSSL mission, it will be the first time in the program's history that a mission launches outside of Florida and California, the company said. Later this year, Rocket Lab will start its first mission for a program of suborbital launches for Space Systems Command's Rocket Systems Launch Program. Most of those will take place from the Pacific Spaceport Complex-Alaska. That same infrastructure can also be used for larger orbital missions in the future. The bottom line: Space superiority isn't possible without launch.

 
 
