 5. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Space Force Tech Sgt. Kyle Yeager adjusts the tilt of a helical antenna in preparation for a training exercise with the AC-130J Ghostrider at Cannon Air Force Base, New Mexico. Photo: Natalie Vandergriff/DVIDS

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🪖 The U.S. Army had a successful demo with Amazon's low Earth orbit satellite network at Maryland's Aberdeen Proving Ground.

 What's next: Amazon and the Army are planning "more advanced tests," the company announced during the AUSA conference this week. 💭 My thought bubble: SpaceX dominates this market. The Army demo gives Amazon steam as it plans to unveil its internet service later this year . 📡 Ukraine's sudden Starlink restrictions are undercutting Ukraine's fight against Russia, my colleague Barak Ravid reports .

 Driving the news: Service partially returned yesterday, but Ukrainian officials want answers. 💭 My thought bubble: The incident shows that Starlink has become a crucial national security asset, and interference can cause havoc. 🆕 Space Force now has its own special operations headquarters, according to an internal memo .

 The big picture: The new component field command will weave the Space Force into more missions. 💭 My thought bubble: Last year, lawmakers questioned the component's standup. It appears that's changed. 
 
